sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant UI as StreamingViewer UI
    participant Pipeline as Display Pipeline
    participant ZEN as ZEN Gateway
    participant Viewer as Napari Viewer
    participant Writer as Configured OME-Zarr Writer
    participant Store as Output Store

    UI->>ZEN: Connect and list experiments without starting acquisition
    UI->>Pipeline: Monitor global pixel stream

    alt Display: start selected experiment
        User->>UI: Select setup and click Start
        UI->>ZEN: Reload XML metadata and prepare experiment
        ZEN-->>UI: Dimensions and experiment ID
        UI->>Pipeline: Arm experiment ID filter
        UI->>ZEN: Start loaded experiment
        UI->>ZEN: Subscribe to status changes
    else Display: watch ZEN experiment
        User->>ZEN: Start experiment independently
        Note over UI,Pipeline: No known ID or expected frame count, channel labels All or 1-16
    end

    opt Either Display mode
        loop Accepted frames
            ZEN-->>Pipeline: FrameData with live S,T,M,Z,C
            Pipeline->>Pipeline: Reject unrelated IDs when filter is armed
            Pipeline->>Viewer: Process frame and emit Qt update
            opt First frame of acquisition
                Viewer->>Viewer: Remove only plugin-owned layers and reset frame storage
            end
            Viewer->>Viewer: Store sparse key S,T,M,Z,C
            Viewer->>Viewer: Update latest 2D preview or optional 7D history
        end
        alt Napari-started experiment finishes
            ZEN-->>UI: Status reports no longer running
            UI->>UI: Wait for expected unique frames or pixel inactivity
            Note over Pipeline,Viewer: Keep global stream and ID filter active during trailing-frame drain
        else ZEN-started experiment finishes or user stops
            UI->>UI: Detect inactivity timeout or handle Stop
        end
        UI->>Viewer: Restructure available frames into STZYX channel mosaics
            Viewer->>Viewer: Place tiles from streamed coordinates, higher M wins overlaps
        UI->>Pipeline: Clear experiment ID filter after final restructure
        UI->>UI: Close progress and restore idle controls
        opt Change Display channel filter
            User->>UI: Select 1-based label or All
            UI->>Pipeline: Restart reader with zero-based channel index
        end
    end

    opt OME-ZARR only instead of Display
        User->>UI: Select setup, writer options and auto-trigger setting, then click Start
        UI->>ZEN: Reload XML dimensions, Z spacing and wells
        UI->>Pipeline: Suspend and close display pixel subscription
        UI->>Writer: Run shared configured writer
        Writer->>ZEN: Open dedicated channel and one pixel stream per source channel
        alt Auto-trigger enabled
            Writer->>ZEN: Prepare and start selected experiment
            ZEN-->>Writer: Target experiment ID
        else Writer armed for manual start
            User->>ZEN: Start intended experiment
            ZEN-->>Writer: First frame pins target experiment ID
        end
        Writer->>Writer: Reject unrelated or missing IDs before decoding
        Writer->>Writer: Validate runtime GRAY8 or GRAY16 payload and native YX shape
        Writer->>ZEN: Query live T,C,Z,S,M counts
        ZEN-->>Writer: Positive live counts, XML counts are fallback
        Writer->>Writer: Build expected T,S,M,C,Z map
        loop Until all expected coordinates arrive or inactivity timeout
            ZEN-->>Writer: FrameData
            Writer->>Writer: Filter IDs, skip duplicate or unexpected coordinates
            Writer->>Writer: Buffer out-of-order frames within configured bound
            Writer->>Store: Append consecutive raw slots or merged HCS scene planes
        end
        Writer->>Store: Drain pending frames, skip missing slots and close writer
        Writer->>Store: Finalize HCS rows or assemble generic TCZYX scene mosaics
        Writer->>Store: Write acquisition_status.json
        alt Acquisition complete
            Writer->>Store: Generate requested pyramids
            Writer-->>UI: Return output path
            UI->>Viewer: Open output with napari-ome-zarr
        else Missing expected coordinates
            Writer-->>UI: Raise IncompleteAcquisitionError with partial path
            UI->>User: Show acquisition warning
            Note over Writer,Store: Retain partial store without pyramids or auto-open, CLI exits nonzero
        end
        UI->>Pipeline: Resume display reader in finally
        UI->>UI: Close progress and restore idle controls
    end

    Note over User,UI: Ready for next acquisition, unrelated layers and docks are preserved